- bbox_3 (bottom-left, y≈397) = 5ma (imidazole-Tr)
- bbox_7 (bottom-right, y≈418) = 5na (proline)

The molecular_recognition SMILES have wildcards/issues. Let me clean them up based on what's drawn (R2 = CH2Ph = benzyl, ester = OBn for all):

- 5ba: R1 = CH2Ph
- 5ia: R1 = CH2C≡CH (propargyl)
- 5ja: R1 = CH2CH2SMe
- 5ka: R1 = CH2CH2CO2Bn
- 5la: R1 = CH2CH2C(=O)NHTr (Tr = trityl = CPh3)
- 5ma: R1 = CH2-(N-trityl-imidazol-4-yl) — histidine with Tr
- 5na: proline residue (cyclic, no Boc-NH freestanding — N is in ring with Boc)

